{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0189e8eFMGSpJw8we3czzr8C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils re-implements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test a spec-driven AI code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: Specs in `docs/specs/` drive code generation into `cmd/<utility>/` packages. Shared libraries (`pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/hashutil`, `pkg/sizeparse`, `pkg/encutil`) provide common infrastructure. Differential tests in each `cmd/` package compare output against `g`-prefixed GNU binaries.\n\n**Implementation state**: Releases 00.0 through 04.1 are partially complete. Most utilities through rel03.1 are implemented. Notable gaps with no ready requirements: cat (rel01.1), nproc (rel03.1), ls (rel04.0), logname (rel04.1). These SRDs have no ready R-items in requirement_states.\n\n**Current focus**: The earliest ready requirements are srd049-realpath R4.2/R4.3 (rel04.1), then all of srd020-echo (rel05.0). Per release-driven priority (P1), realpath comes first, then echo.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n1. **rel04.1 srd049-realpath**: Only R4.2 and R4.3 remain (2 requirements). Everything else is complete per tasks 5242/5243.\n2. **rel05.0 srd020-echo**: All 14 requirements ready (R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.3, R4.1-R4.3). New package -- no contract needed since `cmd/` packages are `main` packages with no exports.\n3. Remaining echo requirements (R4.2, R4.3) deferred to next batch due to 4-task limit.\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\n```\nTask 0: srd049-realpath R4.2 (w=1), R4.3 (w=1)\n  Total weight: 1+1 = 2 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 1: srd020-echo R1.1 (w=1), R1.2 (w=1), R1.3 (w=1), R1.4 (w=1)\n  Total weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 2: srd020-echo R2.1 (w=1), R2.2 (w=1), R2.3 (w=1), R2.4 (w=1)\n  Total weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 3: srd020-echo R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1), R3.3 (w=1), R4.1 (w=1)\n  Total weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/realpath: features implementation (srd049-realpath R4.2, R4.3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd049-realpath.yaml (R4.2 and R4.3 requirements)\n      - cmd/realpath/main.go (existing implementation to extend)\n      - cmd/realpath/realpath_test.go (existing differential tests to extend)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/realpath/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Implement R4.2 and R4.3 features\n      - path: cmd/realpath/realpath_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases for R4.2 and R4.3\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd049-realpath R4.2 -- read the SRD for the exact specification and implement the described behavior\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd049-realpath R4.3 -- read the SRD for the exact specification and implement the described behavior\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Extend the existing cmd/realpath/main.go code structure -- do not restructure or refactor existing code\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests with reference binary grealpath for differential testing\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Call exec.LookPath for grealpath and t.Skip if not found\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"srd049-realpath R4.2 implemented and behavior matches grealpath reference binary\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"srd049-realpath R4.3 implemented and behavior matches grealpath reference binary\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/realpath/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/realpath/ -count=1 passes (or skips gracefully if grealpath not found)\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go 